92186553433 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553433 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553433 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186552973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553433 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "77e677bc-abeb-5bb6-bf03-5c9c94891cbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553460 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553460 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553460 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553460 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553460 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b28e8121-9af9-52a0-b859-1492c6936f8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553486 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9027672-89dd-5956-be1e-019b2d653102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553528 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553528 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269548" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553528 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553528 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector-valued function $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x},$ the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63af40a1-e373-588a-a15a-0cad7e71e5cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553528 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(x)$ where $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the total derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(5{x}_{1}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(5{x}_{1}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(3{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553556 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553556 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553556 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553556 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $f:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{12}}=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553556 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9948bdcd-742f-571f-96d0-1bd2c32c8fbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553556 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{11}+2{a}_{12}+{a}_{13} \\\\ 3{a}_{21}+2{a}_{22}+{a}_{23}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{12}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{13}}(3{a}_{21}+2{a}_{22}+{a}_{23})=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553561 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553561 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269507" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553561 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553561 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{3}.$ What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a75d383a-395b-563b-8f65-088c9a838675" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553561 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f(x)\\in R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553584 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553584 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269557" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553584 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553584 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector-valued function $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}]x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x},$ the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553584 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e86c609f-69e3-5722-94f9-81733ff82960" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553584 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(x)$ where $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the total derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{4}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{4}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(4{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(4{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the total derivative is a constant matrix, evaluating it at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ gives the same matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553591 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553591 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553591 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553591 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $f:{R}^{4\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{32}}=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553591 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ffba6d3e-e7c1-5d0c-b946-5bae6cef7f3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553591 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33} \\\\ {a}_{41} & {a}_{42} & {a}_{43}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}+2{a}_{21}-{a}_{31}+3{a}_{41}\\,\\, & {a}_{12}+2{a}_{22}-{a}_{32}+3{a}_{42}\\,\\, & {a}_{13}+2{a}_{23}-{a}_{33}+3{a}_{43}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{32}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{32}}({a}_{12}+2{a}_{22}-{a}_{32}+3{a}_{42})=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2730df21-8134-5276-86e3-c79ae893587b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553612 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553612 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "362943b2-e925-5fe2-8e78-2502aa139a7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553612 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553614 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553614 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3762ba3c-5626-52d2-b995-1d300ba4677b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553614 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553649 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553649 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "913b1683-8ea1-53ec-9dd2-04758516096c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553649 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553657 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a1cb0590-f2c5-50e3-8083-15ad3151aca2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553561 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
